Brutus is one of the very few fights that are harder in the remakes than they are in the original SNES.  Thin Air only did (Level*2 + 30)* +/-10% in the SNES, but was increased to (Level*2 + 50)* +/-10% in all of the remakes.  Every monster in the game has an internal level, and Brutus's happens to be 5, hence the damage ranges listed in the Attack Patterns.

In any case, you will want to use caution when fighting against him.  On the very 1st turn, Milly will want to use Buff on herself while Nevan Defends.  Then when the 2nd Round comes around, have Milly use Buff on Nevan as he uses the Ghent Staff on her. 

Carver and Amos will want to use Kabuff twice.  After that, Amos and Carver should use Focus Strength + Double-Edged Slash, Milly should Midheal every time Brutus is about to use Thin Air or Multislice, and Buff on every other turn.  As for Nevan, he should just keep spamming the Ghent Staff.  You can occasionally use Frizzle with your mages if you wish to; but it will only do around ~30 Damage a pop with Brutus's resistances.

This is assuming that you have followed the guide to the letter up until now.  If you do not have Buff on most of your characters, you will want to remove Rex's vocation, and have him fill in for Nevan; durability will be at a premium for parties who only have Milly to help with Buffing.  If this is you, let Rex land Sap on Brutus twice to help out Amos and Carver.  In addition, Amos will want the Ghent Staff since Rex and Milly will both be busy slinging their respective spells

== Path to Wayfarer's Pass ==

When all is said and done, talk to the King, then talk to the minister in order to receive an empty casket.  Then go to Wayfarer's Pass.

